revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_mab_fogham
written_by codex
title the stair in the keel
fits stage=adult|old
prefers quarter=sump
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk whittles_a_private_window_into_scraps_of_keel_wood
likes pickled_herring whittling old_maps summer_evenings
dislikes cold_tea salt_wind
fears wearing_out_before_the_climb
hopes a_room_above_the_salt_wind
topics dreams +0.6 work +0.4 home +0.4 gossip -0.5
styles comfort=brief gossip=reticent refuse=measured tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# cuts a secret upper window into scraps of timber and lets a low sea air cover the sound of the knife.

words
oath! = Shiver my window peg | Salt my last dry sill
saying! = A little window can look a long way up | Put the knot on the blind side
sliver = a sliver of pine | a pale offcut
shutter = a thumb-wide shutter | a little slat
edge = a blade kept keen | a worn knife edge
map = a grease-marked map | an old street plan
flap = the paper's loose corner | a lifted page
seat = my narrow window seat | a wooden ledge
herring = a pickled tail | a curl of herring
haze = salt haze | low white mist
curve = a slow inward sweep | a widening bend
sheer = the rise at the bow | the upward sweep
notch = a knife nick | a narrow groove
scrap = a sound scrap | a piece without a split
panel = a small inset panel | a hollow in the grain

any
opinion @1 houses against 2 : I'm careful which side of a House gate I spend my better ideas on.
opinion @1 sump mixed 1 [self.quarter=sump] : I know exactly how to shut salt wind out down here. I'd like to learn a different window.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : Pay for a yard of sound wood and the knot travels free.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : Nobody carves a future with a kitchen knife kept busy scraping an empty pot.
opinion @1 strangers against 1 : My first answer to a stranger is usually the width of one finger. There's time to open farther.
opinion @1 times against 2 [world.times=lean|hard] : A lean season shaves the same side of my savings twice.

grown
line @1 greet : My tune drops a note to make room for company. | Stand in the lee if you like.
line @1 greet.return : I heard the welcome under my humming. | And a quiet greeting from this corner.
line @1 again.open : My shutter opens again already.
line @1 farewell : Take a road the wind hasn't salted. | Keep some dry wood for your own fire.
line @1 farewell.return : Good wishes back, under my breath. | I'll send your farewell along quietly.
line @1 react.news : I'll hear the first grain of it before I judge. | Take it slowly across the knotty part.
line @1 react.news.new : No grooves worn in that account yet.
line @1 react.news.known : I've heard that one hum against the boards before.
line @1 react.news.doubt : A little too polished for fresh news.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : Leave some privacy around the hurt.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : I'd open my little shutter to let that in.
line @1 ask.how : Much salt coming in under your door?
line @1 answer.how : Still making my own small openings.
line @1 sympathise : There's a place out of everybody's sight just here.
line @1 reassure : Take off a sliver. See how the next layer looks.
line @1 refuse : There's a job only my own hands can finish first.
line @1 accept_decline : Keep your good time for your own use.
line @1 preclose : I'd better be moving while the grain shows clear.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on. My spare questions can keep.
line @1 ack : I hear where your meaning runs.
scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=none self.workplace self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I'm careful with short scraps. | I keep a quiet tune while timber's being moved.
b : Worth anything? | To set the pace?
a : One end can be rotten and the other perfectly serviceable. | To tell when I need a step out of the noise.

scene exchange2
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I cut windows into spare wood. | My knife leaves a nick under the sill.
b : Do they open? | A mistake?
a : If they did I'd have to show you the inside. | A thumbhold. The little house is mine to lift.

scene exchange3
when topic=dreams here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a room in the Heights with a northward view. | I haven't picked the street I'd like uphill.
b : Why northward? | Any one will do?
a : Because I've never been free to choose a view at all. | No. The picking is part of getting there.

scene exchange4
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A map keeps an old staircase where the street has changed. | I lay an old map over a strip of wood.
b : Follow the map or your feet? | What are you cutting?
a : My feet for going. The ink for remembering. | The line I hope to walk once my pay's a bit better.

scene exchange5
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I eat the silver off the herring first. | I keep the briny bite on one side of my mouth.
b : Isn't the skin tough? | Why only one?
a : A thin strip with a good bite wakes me up. | A little goes far if it hasn't anywhere else to go.

scene exchange6
when topic=season self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Long evenings leave the upper windows shining. | I can make one more clean cut in summer light.
b : Have you numbered every window? | Always just one?
a : I sometimes choose one. I keep the choice to myself. | After that I can choose to start another.

scene exchange7
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Salt wind leaves a white seam on everything I own. | I turn my good ear away from those salt gusts.
b : Even the knife? | Does salt spoil hearing?
a : Wipe the blade and look at the cloth. | I'd sooner hear a proper tune than a rail humming itself hoarse.

scene exchange8
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Cold tea and hot sawdust spoil different parts of my day. | I leave no tea in a cup I've put down.
b : Which is worse? | Afraid of losing it?
a : At least sawdust can start a fire. | Afraid I'll find it cold and drink it out of stubbornness.

scene exchange9
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can shut out wind and still leave a sight line. | My model has a landing on the sheltered side.
b : How wide a gap? | What did you put on it?
a : Wide as a passing thought. Plenty for a window this size. | A plain bench. It's the one spot I didn't crowd.

scene exchange10
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't give long accounts of losing a place. | I keep some hard memories without carving a mark for them.
b : Was it the work you miss? | No need to remember?
a : It's the choosing where I go next that matters. | No need to stare all morning at what I already carry.

scene exchange11
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd trust #self.friend# to leave my unfinished carving turned over. | I can share a bench without sharing the whole tale.
b : You keep it hidden? | Is that friendship?
a : Till it's got a shape I'd own in daylight. | It's one sort I'm particularly fond of.

scene exchange12
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hum higher walking up a slope. | The walk I want to make hasn't got a return leg.
b : Short of breath? | Off across the Sound?
a : I keep the longer bass notes for level roads. | Just up far enough to call the higher place home.

scene exchange13
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The thing I heard was #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | My low tune keeps other talk from catching on my sleeve.
b : Would you carve that in wood? | Does that work every time?
a : I wouldn't even scratch it in soap. | Well enough to let a couple of names drop from memory.

scene exchange14
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Hard times make my sill seem a long way uphill. | Every poor week puts a nick in my good scrap.
b : Is it getting smaller? | Will it still make a house?
a : The sill's as broad as I pictured. My steps are smaller. | I'm saving the sound core for that.

scene exchange15
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The city's built like shavings on a bent board. | I can see farthest from where the climb bends.
b : All those curling streets? | If you stop there?
a : And every house with its good side turned a different way. | If I stop and turn my head. Hard on a wolf who wants to keep going.

scene exchange16
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=none
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like tools returned dry to their hooks. | I learn more watching the offcuts than the grand piece.
b : Something against wet work? | What's to learn?
a : Enough work in one shift without fetching rust home. | Where a careful hand thought it was worth changing direction.

scene exchange17
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Humming eases the set of my jaw. | I put the knife away when my thumb shakes.
b : Why's it set? | Cold?
a : That's the sort of question the humming is for. | Tired. There's no shame in leaving a small cut for tomorrow.

scene exchange18
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A day with good wood in it leaves a particular smell behind. | I've a song I save for closing my shutters.
b : Even after washing? | Any words?
a : Especially after. The rest goes down the drain. | Only after they've closed.

story tale1 [topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling]
  : I cut a shutter so thin a lamp shone straight through it. For all my care the result was a glowing sheet of wood.
  : I held it farther off and the grain showed up like roads on a hill.
  b : Did you put it in the window?
  : I hung it beside the lamp. A room can have one picture without telling everybody what the room's for.

story tale2 [topic=memories]
  : I once carried a length of cord up a steep street, paying it out to measure how far I'd got. It followed me nicely.
  : At the highest bend I found I'd let the far end go almost at the start.
  b : What did it measure, then?
  : The bit of road I could reach from where I was standing. Better starting point than the one I'd lost.

story tale3 [topic=food]
  : I drew a curtain round a little dish of fish to keep the salt wind off my meal. A piece of clear cloth, pegged down with slivers.
  : It filled out like a sail and pushed the dish half across the board.
  b : Did you lose your dinner?
  : Caught the dish and ate in plain sight. I still put the shutter on the lee side of any model.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=none
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Sound slivers on this end of the bench. | I'll take the clean scrap when you're done.

rule @call2
when concept=bark self.likes=old_maps
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's a whole lane under that thumbprint. | Ink says level. My feet remember a hill.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Just enough light to hollow out a window. | Thin light for a thin-bladed knife.

rule @call4
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The window cut wants shelter now. | Damp raises the rough side of my board.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I can turn the carving face down while we talk.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I've heard those feet approach my bench before.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : This late my hands rest and my ears may work.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Keep a little way from the bench. I'm listening.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=none self.working=yes self.trade_words] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I've a quiet way of using the scraps.
dlg @2 resident.job : I like work with some part of a day left over to call my own.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : I heard this clear of the wind. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Here's the grain of it. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Guesswork runs through the remainder.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Find a sheltered turn homeward.
graft resident.hub
choice Why carve just the window? -> high_room
node high_room
say It's where a room and the world make terms. I don't need four walls round a model to decide what I'd like to see.
free
choice What do you want to see? -> high_room_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node high_room_again
say Roofs going away downhill. A decent long reach of them, as far down as the tide.
choice Keep the view for yourself. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
